-- A count that is known not to be negative.
--
-- `NativeArray.make_*` takes a length the compiler must know is zero or
-- more. For a product or a call's result it cannot work that out, and says
-- so on every build. `Strata.Size.of` gives the same number with that
-- knowledge attached (a negative one becomes zero), so the build is quiet
-- and a wrong length cannot reach the allocator.
mod Strata.Size do

  doc "[n], or 0 if it is negative: a length the compiler knows is not negative."
  fn of(n : Int) : {Int | _ >= 0} do if n >= 0 do n else 0 end end
end
